-- הסכם קיבוצי מיום 16.9.2020 — הסדרים לתקופה מוגבלת נוספת עקב משבר נגיף
-- הקורונה: the public-sector agreement of the second corona lockdown,
-- between the State (and the defence plants), the Centre of Local
-- Government, the three large cities, the regional councils and the
-- religious councils, and the New General Histadrut. Whom it covers, and
-- another public employer under heavier restrictions by an accession
-- letter the Histadrut may object to (§2); its period, 17.9.2020–11.10.2020
-- or the earlier end of the restrictions (§3); the manager and the
-- employee in the arrangement ("עובד בהסדר": groups א'–ג', and who may not
-- be one) (§4); employing as many as possible, at least half at the
-- workplace (§5); notice to the employee and the list to the workers'
-- representatives (§6); the special period — not working, paid a special
-- payment of 70% of the components counted for severance, with its
-- pension, leave, sickness, havraa, clothing and birth-pay rules (§7); the
-- flexibility to employ more — a lower position with a special
-- compensation, other duties, moving, other hours and shifts (§8); new
-- technologies (§9); its end, no §29 approval, renegotiation, the Takshir,
-- no precedent, and the agreements it replaces (§10); rights kept and its
-- priority (§§11–12); the follow-up committee (§13); the pension
-- contributions still negotiated (§14). Annexed: the form of the accession
-- letter.
--
-- It covers no teaching employee: it reaches an employee "represented by
-- the Histadrut" (§2(א)), and the teaching scale is represented by הסתדרות
-- המורים and ארגון המורים (the Collective Agreements Law, §§15–16,
-- imported). Of the agreements its recital names, only the first, of
-- 18.3.2020, is in the corpus, and is imported; the rest — of 13.4, 17.4,
-- 30.4, 1.5, 18.5, 30.6, 16.7 and 4.8.2020 — are outside it, and a rule
-- that needs one of them takes it as an input. The framework of 17.7.2023
-- counts an "עובד בהסדר" of this agreement for its grant, with the share
-- of a position this agreement computes, and imports this file. The
-- teachers' instruments of the same weeks are held against it in
-- l4/tests/2020-21_tashpa_02-tests.l4. It speaks to no pay item of
-- l4/lib/vocabulary.l4 and is in no root.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT budget_foundations_law
IMPORT sick_pay_law
IMPORT `2020-03-18_framework-agreement_public-sector_covid-furlough`

§ `הסכם קיבוצי — הסדרים לתקופה מוגבלת נוספת עקב משבר נגיף הקורונה (16.9.2020)`

DECLARE `2020 arrangement party` IS ONE OF
    `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    `the employee, of 16.9.2020`
    `the Histadrut, of 16.9.2020`
    `the parties, of 16.9.2020`
    `the follow-up committee, of 16.9.2020`

DECLARE `2020 arrangement action` IS ONE OF
    `decide whether the agreement of 16.9.2020 applies to a personal contract`
    `notify the Histadrut of joining the agreement of 16.9.2020`
    `object to an employer joining the agreement of 16.9.2020`
    `discuss the Histadrut's objection to an employer joining`
    `raise a workplace's closing in the follow-up committee of 16.9.2020`
    `employ as many employees as possible in the second lockdown`
    `try to employ more and put fewer in the arrangement`
    `give the employee written notice of the arrangement`
    `give the workers' representatives the list of employees in the arrangement`
    `pay the special payment of 16.9.2020`
    `make the contributions on the special payment of 16.9.2020`
    `pay the grant on return from birth leave, of 16.9.2020`
    `offer a lower position in the employee's own job`
    `raise the lower position again`
    `cut the lower position the employer set`
    `pay the special compensation of 16.9.2020`
    `change the employee's job definitions`
    `undergo the training a change of job needs`
    `move an employee in the arrangement to another job`
    `change the start and end of the working day`
    `call the employee to work on another day of the week`
    `move the employee to shifts`
    `oppose new technologies for the corona crisis`
    `negotiate the changes a significant change in the restrictions needs`
    `decide disputes over the agreement of 16.9.2020 unanimously`
    `negotiate pension contributions on the full salary of an employee in the arrangement`

-- akn:preamble The agreement's frame: a label row with no text of its own.
-- akn:preamble/p1 The registration stamp: registered on 15.12.2020, number 7035 + 367/2020; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p2 The document's title; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p4 "Between"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p10 The employers' short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p11 "On the one side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p12 "And"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 The New General Histadrut and who represents it; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The Histadrut's short name; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p15 "On the other side"; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p16 A recital: fighting the spread of the virus needed special instructions that bear on the whole economy and the public sector.
-- akn:preamble/p17 A recital: those instructions restrict workplaces, employees coming to work and the services to the public, and make ordinary work impossible.
-- akn:preamble/p19 A recital: the crisis going on, the parties set arrangements for a further limited time, given the change the government's second lockdown brings, under the Special Powers Law or its instructions.
-- akn:preamble/p20 A recital: the parties set down their understandings in this collective agreement.
-- akn:preamble/p21 The words of agreement that introduce the clauses; no rule.

-- ¶3: signed on 16 September 2020.
@ref akn:preamble/p3
`the 2020 arrangement agreement was signed on` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 16 9 2020

-- ¶5–¶9: the employers that sign ("המעסיקים"): the State — and, for the
-- defence plants' employees under §2(6) of the State Service
-- (Appointments) Law, those empowered to sign for them; the Centre of
-- Local Government for its members but the three large cities; the three
-- large cities; the Centre of Regional Councils for its members; the
-- religious councils' union.
@ref akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9
`the employers that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020` MEANS
    LIST "מדינת ישראל (לרבות המפעלים הביטחוניים)", "הרשויות המקומיות (מרכז השלטון המקומי)", "שלוש הערים הגדולות",
         "המועצות האזוריות (מרכז המועצות האזוריות)", "המועצות הדתיות"

-- ¶18: the agreements signed in the crisis so far, each with its short
-- name: of 18.3.2020 ("הסכם יציאה לחופשה", imported); 13.4.2020 (its
-- extension); 17.4.2020 ("הסכם המשך יציאה לחופשה"); 30.4.2020 (its
-- extension); 1.5.2020 ("הסכם התו הסגול") and 18.5.2020 (with it, "the
-- purple badge agreement as amended"); 30.6.2020 ("הסכם העדכון");
-- 16.7.2020 ("the follow-up committee on lockdown and closing"); 4.8.2020
-- ("the extension of the purple badge agreement as amended"). All but the
-- first are outside the corpus.
@ref akn:preamble/p18
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 recites the leave agreement of` MEANS `the 2020 furlough agreement was signed on`

`why the crisis agreements of 13.4–4.8.2020 are not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכמים הקיבוציים מיום 13.4.2020, 17.4.2020 (\"הסכם המשך יציאה לחופשה\"), 30.4.2020, 1.5.2020 ו־18.5.2020 (\"הסכם התו הסגול המתוקן\"), 30.6.2020, 16.7.2020 ו־4.8.2020 (\"הסכם הארכה להסכם התו הסגול המתוקן\")"

`why the Special Powers Law is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק סמכויות מיוחדות להתמודדות עם נגיף הקורונה החדש (הוראת שעה), תש\"ף-2020"

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- (א): the preamble is part of it; (ב): the headings are for convenience
-- and teach nothing of its reading.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
`the 2020 arrangement agreement's preamble is part of it` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:art_1__para_b
`the 2020 arrangement agreement's headings bear on its reading` MEANS FALSE

§§ `2 תחולת ההסכם`

-- (א): it applies to every employee of the employers that signed it who is
-- represented by the Histadrut ("עובד"), a personal contract included —
-- in the State, a special contract under §40 of the State Service
-- (Appointments) Law too; but a local authority decides whether it applies
-- to one on a personal contract.
@desc An employee, as far as the agreement of 16.9.2020 asks.
DECLARE `2020 arrangement employee` HAS
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a local authority, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on a personal contract, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his local authority applied it to personal contracts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed by an employer that joined the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an aviation employee, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN @desc "עמ\"י תעופה" as the agreement of 17.4.2020 defines it (outside the corpus)
    `an employee §2(ג)(2) lets his local authority leave out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `his local authority left him out under §2(ג)(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a day-care centre for ages 0–3 agreed on, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on unpaid leave, for 16.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN e IS A `2020 arrangement employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within §2(א) of 16.9.2020` e IF
        e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020`
    AND e's `represented by the Histadrut, for 16.9.2020`
    AND (   NOT (e's `in a local authority, for 16.9.2020` AND e's `on a personal contract, for 16.9.2020`)
         OR e's `his local authority applied it to personal contracts`)

`a local authority's choice for personal contracts` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `decide whether the agreement of 16.9.2020 applies to a personal contract`

-- (ב): it applies also to an employee of another public employer (not a
-- signatory) on or for which restrictions apply beyond the "purple badge"
-- ones in force on 12.9.2020, on the eve of the government's decision on
-- the multi-stage plan, and which signs the accession letter of annex א':
-- (1) the employer notifies the chair of the Histadrut's trade-union
-- department in writing; (2) it is in force from that notice, unless (3)
-- the chair objects within 48 hours — then the parties discuss the
-- objection and the answer to it (the wages commissioner taking part where
-- the employer is a budgeted or supported body under the Budget
-- Foundations Law, imported), "and the parties act by that decision". No
-- decision is named before those words; read as the outcome of the
-- discussion (finding F-framework-2020-09-b), and until there is one the
-- agreement is not in force for that employer.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_b__subpara_3
GIVEN `restrictions beyond the purple badge of 12.9.2020` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed the accession letter and notified the Histadrut` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Histadrut objected within 48 hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the discussion decided it joins` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc NOTHING while the discussion of (3) has decided nothing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employer joins the agreement of 16.9.2020` `restrictions beyond the purple badge of 12.9.2020` `signed the accession letter and notified the Histadrut` `the Histadrut objected within 48 hours` `the discussion decided it joins` IF
        `restrictions beyond the purple badge of 12.9.2020`
    AND `signed the accession letter and notified the Histadrut`
    AND (   NOT `the Histadrut objected within 48 hours`
         OR `the discussion decided it joins` EQUALS JUST TRUE)

`notifying the Histadrut of joining` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `notify the Histadrut of joining the agreement of 16.9.2020`

`objecting to an employer joining` MEANS
    PARTY `the Histadrut, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `object to an employer joining the agreement of 16.9.2020`
    HENCE (PARTY `the parties, of 16.9.2020`
           MUST  `discuss the Histadrut's objection to an employer joining`)

`the hours the Histadrut has to object` MEANS 48

-- What (3) names before "the parties act by that decision": a notice, an
-- objection and a discussion — no decision.
`what §2(ב)(3) of 16.9.2020 names before "that decision"` MEANS
    LIST "הודעה על התנגדות", "דיון בטענות ובמענה"

`the decision (3) of 16.9.2020 says the parties act by, as printed` MEANS
    NOT elem "החלטה" `what §2(ב)(3) of 16.9.2020 names before "that decision"`

-- (ג): notwithstanding, it does not apply to (1) an aviation employee as
-- the agreement of 17.4.2020 defines him; (2) where a local authority has
-- 14 or more working days in the period, it may leave out an employee the
-- agreement of 17.4.2020 did not reach, and one not entitled to tenure or
-- not yet past the period that earns it (which those are is an input);
-- (3) employees of day-care centres for ages 0–3 in the authorities agreed
-- on; (4) for the avoidance of doubt, an employee while on unpaid leave —
-- and no employer must bring one back from unpaid leave at the signing.
@ref akn:art_2__para_c akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_c__subpara_4
GIVEN e IS A `2020 arrangement employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `left out by §2(ג) of 16.9.2020` e IF
       e's `an aviation employee, for 16.9.2020`
    OR (e's `an employee §2(ג)(2) lets his local authority leave out` AND e's `his local authority left him out under §2(ג)(2)`)
    OR e's `in a day-care centre for ages 0–3 agreed on, for 16.9.2020`
    OR e's `on unpaid leave, for 16.9.2020`

GIVEN `working days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a local authority may leave employees out under §2(ג)(2)` `working days in the period` IF
    `working days in the period` AT LEAST 14

GIVEN e IS A `2020 arrangement employee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 16.9.2020 covers` e IF
        (`within §2(א) of 16.9.2020` e OR e's `employed by an employer that joined the agreement of 16.9.2020`)
    AND NOT `left out by §2(ג) of 16.9.2020` e

-- The same, as the Collective Agreements Law asks it (§§15–16): it does
-- not reach a kind of employee the Histadrut does not represent — a
-- teaching employee among them, whoever employs him.
GIVEN e IS A `2020 arrangement employee`
GIVETH AN `employee a collective agreement may reach`
DECIDE `the 2020 arrangement employee, as the law asks` e IS
    `employee a collective agreement may reach` WITH
        `his employer is a party to the agreement`  IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020`
        `his employer is represented for it by an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020`
        `his employer was or became a member of an employers' organisation that is a party` IS e's `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020`
        `his employer was expressly left out of the agreement` IS FALSE
        `he is of a kind of employee the agreement includes` IS e's `represented by the Histadrut, for 16.9.2020`
        `he is in an occupation or post the agreement includes` IS TRUE

§§ `3 תקופת ההסכם`

-- A temporary emergency period from 17.9.2020 to 11.10.20, unless the
-- restrictions on workplaces under the Special Powers Law, or another law
-- setting them, are lifted earlier — then it ends when they are lifted
-- ("תקופת ההסכם").
@ref akn:art_3/p1
`the 2020 arrangement period begins` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 17 9 2020

GIVEN `the restrictions were lifted on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the 2020 arrangement period ends` `the restrictions were lifted on` IS
    CONSIDER `the restrictions were lifted on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2020
    WHEN JUST l THEN (IF l `is on or before` (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2020) THEN l ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2020)

GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the restrictions were lifted on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the 2020 arrangement period` d `the restrictions were lifted on` IF
        d `is on or after` `the 2020 arrangement period begins`
    AND d `is on or before` `the 2020 arrangement period ends` `the restrictions were lifted on`

§§ `4 הגדרות`

-- akn:art_4/p1 "In this agreement": introduces the definitions; no rule.

-- "מנהל": (1) in the civil service, the director-general of the ministry or
-- auxiliary unit; (2) in a local authority, its head, director-general or
-- secretary as the head empowers; (3) in an institution of higher
-- education, its director-general; (4) in a religious council, its chair;
-- (5) at another public employer, its director-general or the like, or the
-- most senior office-holder. No approval is asked of anyone, where the
-- agreement of 18.3.2020 asked one of each.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_1 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_2 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_3 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_4 akn:art_4__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN e IS AN `employer of 18.3.2020`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the manager of 16.9.2020` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the civil service, of 18.3.2020` THEN "מנכ\"ל המשרד הממשלתי או יחידת הסמך"
    WHEN `a local authority, of 18.3.2020` THEN "ראש הרשות המקומית, מנכ\"ל הרשות או מזכירה, לפי הסמכת ראש הרשות"
    WHEN `an institution of higher education, of 18.3.2020` THEN "מנכ\"ל המוסד להשכלה גבוהה"
    WHEN `a religious council, of 18.3.2020` THEN "יו\"ר המועצה הדתית"
    OTHERWISE "המנכ\"ל, בעל תפקיד מקביל, או בעל התפקיד הבכיר ביותר בהנהלה"

-- "עובד בהסדר": one the manager decided, at his discretion and subject to
-- the law, meets both of these in all or part of the period: (1) one of —
-- (א) he cannot go on working as usual because of restrictions set by or
-- under the law, a limit on employees at a workplace among them ("group
-- A"); (ב) he cannot do his work because a decision closed his workplace
-- for an outbreak, to protect the employees and limit the spread ("group
-- B"); (ג) he is not needed at work because restrictions by or under the
-- law brought a significant fall in activity against the eve of the crisis
-- ("group C"); and (2) the employer decided he cannot work other than from
-- his usual workplace (home included), by its rules.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_2 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_2__para_1__subpara_a akn:art_4__hc_2__para_1__subpara_b akn:art_4__hc_2__para_1__subpara_c akn:art_4__hc_2__para_2
DECLARE `group of 16.9.2020` IS ONE OF
    `group A, of 16.9.2020`
    `group B, of 16.9.2020`
    `group C, of 16.9.2020`
    `no group, of 16.9.2020`

@desc An employee on a day of the period, as far as the definition of "עובד בהסדר" asks.
DECLARE `day of an employee, of 16.9.2020` HAS
    `the manager's group for the day` IS A `group of 16.9.2020`
    `the employer decided he cannot work from elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a kindergarten assistant notice 17/2020 reaches` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the month his employment is to end` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in isolation he was bound to at the signing or the closing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sick under a note issued before the signing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on unpaid leave, birth and parenthood included, on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a day of the concentrated Sukkot leave` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ¶ after (2): notwithstanding, a kindergarten assistant in a local
-- authority to whom §1 of employees' notice 17/2020 of 16.9.2020 applies
-- is not set in the arrangement (the notice is outside the corpus); nor is
-- an employee (1) in the month his employment is to end; (2) bound to
-- isolation under the Public Health Order at the signing or the closing,
-- while he is; (3) sick under a note issued before the signing, for its
-- whole term; (4) on unpaid leave, the Women's Work Law's included (and
-- one may still ask for unpaid leave in full, by the employer's rules);
-- (5) on the days of a concentrated Sukkot leave, which nothing here
-- changes, its charging of the balance included.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1 akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1__para_1 akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1__para_2 akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1__para_3 akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1__para_4 akn:art_4__hc_2__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN d IS A `day of an employee, of 16.9.2020`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an employee in the arrangement on the day` d IF
        NOT (d's `the manager's group for the day` EQUALS `no group, of 16.9.2020`)
    AND d's `the employer decided he cannot work from elsewhere`
    AND NOT d's `a kindergarten assistant notice 17/2020 reaches`
    AND NOT d's `in the month his employment is to end`
    AND NOT d's `in isolation he was bound to at the signing or the closing`
    AND NOT d's `sick under a note issued before the signing`
    AND NOT d's `on unpaid leave, birth and parenthood included, on the day`
    AND NOT d's `a day of the concentrated Sukkot leave`

`why employees' notice 17/2020 is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "הודעה בענייני עובדים מספר 17/2020 מיום 16.9.2020 (מרכז השלטון המקומי), סעיף 1"

-- ¶2: where the Histadrut has claims on a decision under (1)(ב), a
-- closing, it may raise its consequences for the employees in the
-- follow-up committee.
@ref akn:art_4__hc_2/p2
`raising a closing in the follow-up committee` MEANS
    PARTY `the Histadrut, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `raise a workplace's closing in the follow-up committee of 16.9.2020`

§§ `5 מתווה להעסקת עובדים`

-- ¶1: as a rule the public employers employ as many employees as are
-- needed and possible, at the workplace or not, within the restrictions.
-- (א) First, as many as possible at the workplace, at 50% or more,
-- priority there going to those who cannot work from home, and as many as
-- possible from elsewhere; ¶2: but where restrictions bring a significant
-- fall in activity, as many as needed. (ב) Second, a reasonable effort to
-- use this agreement's tools — moving an employee among them — to employ
-- more and put fewer in the arrangement. ¶2 of §5: a restriction on a
-- workplace does not stop the employer employing an employee there as far
-- as the restrictions allow (maintenance, for one).
@ref akn:art_5/p1 akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_a/p2
`employing as many as possible` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `employ as many employees as possible in the second lockdown`

GIVEN `employees at the workplace` IS A NUMBER, `employees` IS A NUMBER, `a significant fall in activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§5(א) of 16.9.2020 is met at the workplace` `employees at the workplace` `employees` `a significant fall in activity` IF
       `a significant fall in activity`
    OR `employees at the workplace` AT LEAST (50% TIMES `employees`)

@ref akn:art_5__para_b
`trying to employ more` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `try to employ more and put fewer in the arrangement`

@ref akn:art_5/p2
`a restriction on a workplace stops the employer employing there as allowed` MEANS FALSE

§§ `6 הודעה לעובד בהסדר`

-- (א): an employee set in the arrangement is told so in writing by the day
-- before he moves into it at the latest, or soon after a closing, with the
-- days and his group. (ב): three days after that, the employer gives the
-- workers' representatives the list of employees in the arrangement and
-- their groups. (ג): the same for employees added later.
@ref akn:art_6__para_a akn:art_6__para_c
`telling the employee of the arrangement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `give the employee written notice of the arrangement`

@ref akn:art_6__para_b
`giving the representatives the list` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `give the workers' representatives the list of employees in the arrangement`
    WITHIN 3

§§ `7 תקופה מיוחדת לעובד בהסדר`

-- ¶1: an employee in the arrangement, on his days in it, is not asked to
-- do his job and is paid for that special period ("התקופה המיוחדת") as
-- below. (א): a special payment, paid with the monthly salary; ¶2: it is
-- the product of (א) 70% of the components of his pay counted for the
-- severance completion in his last work month, save havraa and clothing;
-- (ב) the share of the special period in the work month it falls in; (ג)
-- his position — for a part-time employee, the average of December 2019
-- and January–February 2020, of those months he was not in an
-- arrangement; if he worked none of them, the average of the three work
-- months before this period in which he was not in an arrangement under
-- this agreement or the extension of 4.8.2020. ¶: "the last work month" is
-- the work month before this period in which he was in no arrangement
-- under either. Which month that is, and its components, are inputs.
@ref akn:art_7/p1 akn:art_7__para_a akn:art_7__para_a/p2 akn:art_7__para_a__subpara_a akn:art_7__para_a__subpara_b akn:art_7__para_a__subpara_c akn:art_7__para_a__hc_1
`the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020` MEANS 70%

GIVEN `full-time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his position` IS A NUMBER
      `his positions in December 2019 to February 2020 outside an arrangement` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `his positions in the three work months before outside an arrangement` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of a position for the special payment of 16.9.2020` `full-time` `his position` `his positions in December 2019 to February 2020 outside an arrangement` `his positions in the three work months before outside an arrangement` IS
    IF `full-time` THEN `his position`
    ELSE IF NOT null `his positions in December 2019 to February 2020 outside an arrangement`
         THEN sum `his positions in December 2019 to February 2020 outside an arrangement`
              DIVIDED BY count `his positions in December 2019 to February 2020 outside an arrangement`
         ELSE IF NOT null `his positions in the three work months before outside an arrangement`
              THEN sum `his positions in the three work months before outside an arrangement`
                   DIVIDED BY count `his positions in the three work months before outside an arrangement`
              ELSE 0

GIVEN `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing` IS A NUMBER
      `days of the special period in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `days of the work month` IS A NUMBER
      `the share of a position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special payment of 16.9.2020` `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing` `days of the special period in the month` `days of the work month` `the share of a position` IS
    `the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020`
    TIMES `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing`
    TIMES (`days of the special period in the month` DIVIDED BY `days of the work month`)
    TIMES `the share of a position`

`paying the special payment` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `pay the special payment of 16.9.2020`

-- (ב): for the students' scale under the agreement of 1.6.2020 (outside
-- the corpus), the position is the average of the hours actually worked in
-- the three fullest work months of August 2019–August 2020.
@ref akn:art_7__para_b
GIVEN `the hours of the three fullest months of August 2019–August 2020` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the hours of a full position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a student's share of a position for the special payment` `the hours of the three fullest months of August 2019–August 2020` `the hours of a full position` IS
    sum `the hours of the three fullest months of August 2019–August 2020` DIVIDED BY 3 DIVIDED BY `the hours of a full position`

`why the students' agreement of 1.6.2020 is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "ההסכם הקיבוצי בעניין הסטודנטים מיום 1.6.2020"

-- (ג): his leave balance is not charged for the days of the special period.
@ref akn:art_7__para_c
`the special period of 16.9.2020 is charged to the leave balance` MEANS FALSE

-- (ד): for the State Service (Pensions) Law and the old pension funds'
-- position, the special period of one full-time in the month before counts
-- as work at a 70% position; for a part-time one, his position times 70%.
@ref akn:art_7__para_d
GIVEN `his position in the last work month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pension position of the special period, of 16.9.2020` `his position in the last work month` IS
    `his position in the last work month` TIMES `the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020`

-- (ה): its days count for seniority and continuity, by the civil service's
-- rules, or the other employers' own.
@ref akn:art_7__para_e
`the special period of 16.9.2020 counts for seniority and continuity` MEANS TRUE

-- (ו): study-fund contributions are made on the special payment (for those
-- owed them), and pension contributions for one not on a budgetary
-- pension, by the rules for the salary counted for severance.
@ref akn:art_7__para_f
GIVEN `owed study-fund contributions` IS A BOOLEAN, `on a budgetary pension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the contributions on the special payment of 16.9.2020` `owed study-fund contributions` `on a budgetary pension` IS
    IF `owed study-fund contributions`
    THEN (IF `on a budgetary pension` THEN LIST "קרן השתלמות" ELSE LIST "קרן השתלמות", "קופת גמל לקצבה")
    ELSE (IF `on a budgetary pension` THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST "קופת גמל לקצבה")

`making the contributions on the special payment` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `make the contributions on the special payment of 16.9.2020`

-- (ז): one who reports a sick day in the period, with an accrued balance,
-- has sick pay no higher than the special payment for each such day, by
-- his employer's rules; each day of the note takes 70% of a day off his
-- accrued sick days.
@ref akn:art_7__para_g
GIVEN `sick pay he would have` IS A NUMBER, `the special payment for the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick pay in the special period, of 16.9.2020` `sick pay he would have` `the special payment for the day` IS
    min `sick pay he would have` `the special payment for the day`

GIVEN `days of the note` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days taken off the balance, of 16.9.2020` `days of the note` IS
    `days of the note` TIMES `the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020`

-- The Sick Pay Law (imported), §§1 and 5. Sick pay in the period is a
-- collective agreement's — this one's — so §1 leaves the employee out of
-- "an employee" and §§2 to 6 do not reach him; compared all the same, (ז)
-- gives what §5 measures. §5 pays the wage he would have had had he gone on
-- working, which in the special period is the special payment; (ז) pays
-- the lower of his sick pay and that payment — the payment itself whenever
-- it is the lower, as it is when it is 70% of the components. The floor
-- is met.
`sick pay in the special period is the Sick Pay Law's measure` MEANS
        NOT `an employee as section 1 of the Sick Pay Law means` TRUE
    AND `sick pay in the special period, of 16.9.2020` 500 350 AT LEAST `sick pay section 5 gives` 350
#ASSERT `sick pay in the special period is the Sick Pay Law's measure`

-- (ח): for havraa and clothing he is as though he had gone on working.
@ref akn:art_7__para_h
`havraa and clothing of 16.9.2020 are as though he worked` MEANS TRUE

-- (ט): an employee whose birth pay is computed over a time that includes
-- the special period has, on returning to work, a one-time grant of 42.86%
-- of the special payment he was owed; no provident contributions on it.
-- 42.86% of 70% is the 30% the special payment fell short of the salary,
-- to the hundredth of a percent.
@ref akn:art_7__para_i
`the birth-pay grant's rate of 16.9.2020` MEANS 42.86%

GIVEN `the special payment he was owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the birth-pay grant of 16.9.2020` `the special payment he was owed` IS
    `the birth-pay grant's rate of 16.9.2020` TIMES `the special payment he was owed`

`paying the birth-pay grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `pay the grant on return from birth leave, of 16.9.2020`

§§ `8 גמישות העסקה מיוחדת`

-- ¶1: given the crisis, to employ more and put fewer in the arrangement,
-- the employer may make all or some of these changes.
@ref akn:art_8/p1
`the changes of §8 of 16.9.2020 are the employer's to make` MEANS TRUE

-- (א) (the heading: a special period for an employee in the arrangement
-- employed at a lower position) ¶2: to employ more, for employees in the
-- arrangement: (1) (the heading: changing the position) (א) the employer
-- may offer one a position lower than his own, for all or part of the
-- period — part of a day or some days — (1) in his own job only; (2) at
-- 20% or more; (3) no less than half his daily standard hours on each day
-- he is called. (ב) It may raise it later as work needs, within those
-- terms; (ג) and may not lower what it set without his consent. The text
-- numbers the next paragraph (4): no (2) or (3) is in the corpus.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a akn:art_8__para_a/p2 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_a__pnt_1 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_a__pnt_2 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_a__pnt_3
GIVEN `in his own job` IS A BOOLEAN, `the position offered` IS A NUMBER, `his position` IS A NUMBER
      `the least hours on a day he is called` IS A NUMBER, `his daily standard hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a lower position §8(א) of 16.9.2020 allows` `in his own job` `the position offered` `his position` `the least hours on a day he is called` `his daily standard hours` IF
        `in his own job`
    AND `the position offered` AT LEAST 20%
    AND `the position offered` LESS THAN `his position`
    AND `the least hours on a day he is called` AT LEAST (`his daily standard hours` DIVIDED BY 2)

`offering a lower position` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `offer a lower position in the employee's own job`

@ref akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_b
`raising the lower position` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `raise the lower position again`

@ref akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_1__cls_c
`not cutting the lower position` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    SHANT `cut the lower position the employer set`

-- (4) (the heading: what an employee whose position is changed is paid)
-- (א): his salary by the position set. (ב): for the cut, besides his
-- salary, (1) for each month of the period at that position a special
-- compensation; ¶2: the product of (א) 70% of the components counted for
-- the severance completion in his last work month, save havraa and
-- clothing; (ב) the share of the time at that position in the work month;
-- (ג) the difference between his position in the last work month and the
-- weighted position set for him that month ("the rate of the cut"); ¶:
-- "the last work month" as in §7.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_a akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1/p2 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1__pnt_a akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1__pnt_b akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1__pnt_c akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_1__hc_1
GIVEN `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing` IS A NUMBER
      `the share of the month at the lower position` IS A NUMBER
      `his position in the last work month` IS A NUMBER
      `the weighted position set for the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the special compensation of 16.9.2020` `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing` `the share of the month at the lower position` `his position in the last work month` `the weighted position set for the month` IS
    `the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020`
    TIMES `the severance components of the last work month, save havraa and clothing`
    TIMES `the share of the month at the lower position`
    TIMES `not below zero` (`his position in the last work month` MINUS `the weighted position set for the month`)

`paying the special compensation` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `pay the special compensation of 16.9.2020`

-- (2) (and its ¶2): for each such month his position is taken as raised by
-- the rate of the cut times 70%, counted as service for every purpose for
-- the Pensions Law and the old funds' position ("the raise of the
-- position"); his position for those is what he worked plus that raise.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_2 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_2/p2
GIVEN `the weighted position set for the month` IS A NUMBER, `his position in the last work month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pension position of a lower position, of 16.9.2020` `the weighted position set for the month` `his position in the last work month` IS
    `the weighted position set for the month`
    PLUS `the special payment's rate of 16.9.2020` TIMES `not below zero` (`his position in the last work month` MINUS `the weighted position set for the month`)

-- (3): the contributions on the special compensation as on the special
-- payment (§7(ו)). (4): sick pay in proportion, no more than for his actual
-- position plus the compensation, a proportional day off his balance.
-- (5): havraa and clothing as at his usual position. (6): birth pay over a
-- time with the lower position: the grant of 42.86% of the compensation,
-- with no provident contributions.
@ref akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_3 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_4 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_5 akn:art_8__para_a__subpara_4__cls_b__pnt_6
GIVEN `the special compensation he was owed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the birth-pay grant on the compensation, of 16.9.2020` `the special compensation he was owed` IS
    `the birth-pay grant of 16.9.2020` `the special compensation he was owed`

GIVEN `sick pay at his usual position` IS A NUMBER, `the share his actual position and the compensation make of it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick pay at a lower position, of 16.9.2020` `sick pay at his usual position` `the share his actual position and the compensation make of it` IS
    `sick pay at his usual position` TIMES (min 1 `the share his actual position and the compensation make of it`)

-- (ב) (the heading: changing job definitions and tasks) ¶2: for an
-- employee it covers, (1) the employer may change his job's definitions —
-- fewer or new tasks, another place, any change, even outside his
-- occupation; (2) a change of place minds his needs and is near his usual
-- place or his home, as far as possible; (3) a change minds his education
-- and skills and like occupations, as far as possible; (4) he does the
-- training the change needs, at the employer's expense; (5) all with no
-- supplement to his pay.
@ref akn:art_8__para_b akn:art_8__para_b/p2 akn:art_8__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_8__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_8__para_b__subpara_3
`changing the job definitions` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `change the employee's job definitions`

@ref akn:art_8__para_b__subpara_4
`training for the changed job` MEANS
    PARTY `the employee, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `undergo the training a change of job needs`

@ref akn:art_8__para_b__subpara_5
`a change of job of 16.9.2020 carries a pay supplement` MEANS FALSE

-- (ג) (the heading: moving an employee in the arrangement to another job)
-- ¶2: the Histadrut agrees to moving one, by the employer's mobility rules
-- or with his consent, to a job the employer thinks possible and fitting.
@ref akn:art_8__para_c akn:art_8__para_c/p2
`moving to another job` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `move an employee in the arrangement to another job`

-- (ד) (the heading: changing hours and arrangements) ¶2: for an employee
-- it covers, one in the arrangement too: (1) changing the start and end of
-- his day, without splitting it or changing his position (taking nothing
-- from (א)); (2) calling one on a five-day week to work another day —
-- Friday among them (or Friday, Saturday or Sunday outside the Jewish
-- sector) — in place of a day of the same week; ¶2: with no supplement for
-- the day, Takshir 27.2 or any like arrangement notwithstanding; (3) the
-- weekly quota of hours is not exceeded (א), the day before his day of rest
-- is as §2(ב) of the Hours of Work and Rest Law sets (ב), and nothing here
-- derogates from that law (ג); (4) moving him to shifts, even where none
-- are usual, with no supplement for it (Takshir 27.6 notwithstanding) —
-- but one on shifts on the eve of the leave agreement keeps his shift
-- supplement.
@ref akn:art_8__para_d akn:art_8__para_d/p2 akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_1
`changing the hours` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `change the start and end of the working day`

@ref akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_2 akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_2/p2
`calling to work another day` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `call the employee to work on another day of the week`

`a day worked in place of another, of 16.9.2020, carries a supplement` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_3 akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_3__cls_a akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_3__cls_b akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_3__cls_c
GIVEN `hours worked in the week` IS A NUMBER, `his weekly quota` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `another day of 16.9.2020 keeps the weekly quota` `hours worked in the week` `his weekly quota` IF
    `hours worked in the week` AT MOST `his weekly quota`

`why the Hours of Work and Rest Law is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק שעות עבודה ומנוחה, התשי\"א-1951, סעיף 2(ב)"

`why the Takshir is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "תקנון שירות המדינה (תקשי\"ר), פרקי משנה 27.2 ו־27.6"

@ref akn:art_8__para_d__subpara_4
`moving to shifts` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `move the employee to shifts`

GIVEN `on shifts with a supplement on the eve of the leave agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a shift supplement in the period of 16.9.2020` `on shifts with a supplement on the eve of the leave agreement` IF
    `on shifts with a supplement on the eve of the leave agreement`

§§ `9–14 טכנולוגיות, כללי, שמירת זכויות, עדיפות, חילוקי דעות ומשא ומתן`

-- §9: the Histadrut is for the new technologies the service needs for the
-- crisis and will raise no claim against them.
@ref akn:art_9/p1
`not opposing the new technologies` MEANS
    PARTY `the Histadrut, of 16.9.2020`
    SHANT `oppose new technologies for the corona crisis`

-- §10(א): every provision stops at the end of the period, and the
-- agreements, arrangements and practices it changed apply again.
@ref akn:art_10__para_a
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the restrictions were lifted on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement of 16.9.2020 applies on` d `the restrictions were lifted on` IF
    `in the 2020 arrangement period` d `the restrictions were lifted on`

-- (ב): it is no approval under §29 of the Budget Foundations Law
-- (imported).
@ref akn:art_10__para_b
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 is a §29 approval` MEANS FALSE

-- (ג): a significant easing or tightening of the restrictions during it
-- sends the parties to negotiate the changes it needs.
@ref akn:art_10__para_c
`renegotiating on a change in the restrictions` MEANS
    PARTY `the parties, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `negotiate the changes a significant change in the restrictions needs`

-- (ד): it changes no normative standing of the Takshir or what it names,
-- and naming them applies them to no employer they do not bind. (ה): signed
-- in exceptional circumstances, it is no precedent.
@ref akn:art_10__para_d
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 changes the Takshir's standing` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:art_10__para_e
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 is a precedent` MEANS FALSE

-- (ו): it replaces the purple-badge agreement as amended (as its extension
-- of 4.8.2020 worded it) and the follow-up committee's provisions on
-- lockdown and closing, "from its start as set out in §2 above", with no
-- double payment. §2 sets no start for a signatory — §3 does, 17.9.2020 —
-- but it does for an employer that joins, the day of its notice
-- (§2(ב)(2)); read so that the reference does something (convention
-- reading.every-word; finding F-framework-2020-09-a): the replacement runs
-- from the day the agreement starts for that employer.
@ref akn:art_10__para_f
GIVEN `the employer joined by notice on` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc NOTHING for an employer that signed
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the agreement of 16.9.2020 replaces the earlier ones from` `the employer joined by notice on` IS
    CONSIDER `the employer joined by notice on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the 2020 arrangement period begins`
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

`§2 of 16.9.2020 sets a start for a signatory` MEANS FALSE

-- §11 ¶1: it changes the agreements, arrangements and practices only as
-- it says expressly; ¶2: it takes no right a party would have had but for
-- it, but on the matters it settles expressly it governs.
@ref akn:art_11/p1 akn:art_11/p2
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 changes only what it says expressly` MEANS TRUE

-- §12: its provisions prevail over any other, in another agreement or
-- arrangement, collective or personal. Within its parties' own agreements,
-- that is the precedence of a later special provision; it reaches no
-- agreement of another union, which it does not bind.
@ref akn:art_12/p1
`the agreement of 16.9.2020 prevails over its parties' other provisions` MEANS TRUE

-- §13: a follow-up committee of the wages commissioner, the chair of the
-- trade-union department (or their delegates) and a representative of the
-- local authorities (where they are concerned) follows it and decides
-- disputes over it unanimously; its decisions are final and bind.
@ref akn:art_13/p1
`the 2020 arrangement follow-up committee` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee, of 16.9.2020`
    MAY   `decide disputes over the agreement of 16.9.2020 unanimously`

-- §14: following §4(ד) of the extension of 4.8.2020 (outside the corpus),
-- the negotiation goes on over the Histadrut's demand that the provident
-- contributions of an employee in the arrangement be on his full salary,
-- from 1 May 2020.
@ref akn:art_14
`negotiating contributions on the full salary` MEANS
    PARTY `the parties, of 16.9.2020`
    MUST  `negotiate pension contributions on the full salary of an employee in the arrangement`

`the full-salary contributions are demanded from` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 2020

