    `in a day-care centre for ages 0–3 agreed on, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `on unpaid leave, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
`a teacher of the State in September 2020` MEANS `2020 arrangement employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS TRUE
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `in a local authority, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `on a personal contract, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `his local authority applied it to personal contracts` IS FALSE
    `employed by an employer that joined the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `an aviation employee, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `an employee §2(ג)(2) lets his local authority leave out` IS FALSE
    `his local authority left him out under §2(ג)(2)` IS FALSE
    `in a day-care centre for ages 0–3 agreed on, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `on unpaid leave, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
`a personal contract of a local authority in September 2020` MEANS `2020 arrangement employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS TRUE
    `represented by the Histadrut, for 16.9.2020` IS TRUE
    `in a local authority, for 16.9.2020` IS TRUE
    `on a personal contract, for 16.9.2020` IS TRUE
    `his local authority applied it to personal contracts` IS FALSE
    `employed by an employer that joined the agreement of 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `an aviation employee, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `an employee §2(ג)(2) lets his local authority leave out` IS FALSE
    `his local authority left him out under §2(ג)(2)` IS FALSE
    `in a day-care centre for ages 0–3 agreed on, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE
    `on unpaid leave, for 16.9.2020` IS FALSE

-- §2: the clerk is in it, a State teacher is not (by the agreement and by
-- the law), and a local authority's personal contract only if the
-- authority applies it.
#ASSERT `the agreement of 16.9.2020 covers` `a clerk of the State in September 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 16.9.2020 covers` `a teacher of the State in September 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the agreement of 16.9.2020 covers` `a personal contract of a local authority in September 2020`
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a general collective agreement` (`the 2020 arrangement employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in September 2020`)
#ASSERT NOT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2020 arrangement employee, as the law asks` `a teacher of the State in September 2020`)
#ASSERT `the collective agreement applies to the employee` `a special collective agreement` (`the 2020 arrangement employee, as the law asks` `a clerk of the State in September 2020`)

-- §2(ב): an employer under heavier restrictions joins on notice; on an
-- objection, only by the decision; §2(ג)(2) from 14 working days.
#ASSERT `an employer joins the agreement of 16.9.2020` TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `an employer joins the agreement of 16.9.2020` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING
#ASSERT `an employer joins the agreement of 16.9.2020` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `an employer joins the agreement of 16.9.2020` FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING
#ASSERT `a local authority may leave employees out under §2(ג)(2)` 14
#ASSERT NOT `a local authority may leave employees out under §2(ג)(2)` 13

-- §3: to 11.10.2020; to 1.10.2020 if the restrictions are lifted then.
#ASSERT `the 2020 arrangement period ends` NOTHING EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2020
#ASSERT `the 2020 arrangement period ends` (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2020)) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2020
#ASSERT NOT `in the 2020 arrangement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 10 2020) (JUST (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2020))
#ASSERT `in the 2020 arrangement period` (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2020) NOTHING

-- §4: group B with no way to work from elsewhere is in the arrangement; in
-- isolation, or on a Sukkot leave day, he is not.
`a closed workplace's day` MEANS `day of an employee, of 16.9.2020` WITH
    `the manager's group for the day` IS `group B, of 16.9.2020`
    `the employer decided he cannot work from elsewhere` IS TRUE
    `a kindergarten assistant notice 17/2020 reaches` IS FALSE
    `in the month his employment is to end` IS FALSE
    `in isolation he was bound to at the signing or the closing` IS FALSE
    `sick under a note issued before the signing` IS FALSE
    `on unpaid leave, birth and parenthood included, on the day` IS FALSE
    `a day of the concentrated Sukkot leave` IS FALSE
`a Sukkot leave day` MEANS `day of an employee, of 16.9.2020` WITH
    `the manager's group for the day` IS `group B, of 16.9.2020`
    `the employer decided he cannot work from elsewhere` IS TRUE
    `a kindergarten assistant notice 17/2020 reaches` IS FALSE
    `in the month his employment is to end` IS FALSE
    `in isolation he was bound to at the signing or the closing` IS FALSE
    `sick under a note issued before the signing` IS FALSE
    `on unpaid leave, birth and parenthood included, on the day` IS FALSE
    `a day of the concentrated Sukkot leave` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `an employee in the arrangement on the day` `a closed workplace's day`
#ASSERT NOT `an employee in the arrangement on the day` `a Sukkot leave day`
#ASSERT `§5(א) of 16.9.2020 is met at the workplace` 50 100 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `§5(א) of 16.9.2020 is met at the workplace` 49 100 FALSE
#ASSERT `the manager of 16.9.2020` `the civil service, of 18.3.2020` EQUALS "מנכ\"ל המשרד הממשלתי או יחידת הסמך"

-- §7: components of 10,000, 15 of 30 days, a full position: 3,500. A
-- part-time employee of 50%, 60% and 70% in December–February: 60%; with
-- none of those months, the three before. Pension position 70% of his
-- own; 10 sick days take 7. The birth-pay grant restores the special
-- payment to the salary within a hundredth of a percent.
#ASSERT `the special payment of 16.9.2020` 10000 15 30 1 EQUALS 3500
#ASSERT `the share of a position for the special payment of 16.9.2020` FALSE 1 (LIST (50%), (60%), (70%)) EMPTY EQUALS 60%
#ASSERT `the share of a position for the special payment of 16.9.2020` FALSE 1 EMPTY (LIST (40%), (40%), (40%)) EQUALS 40%
#ASSERT `the share of a position for the special payment of 16.9.2020` TRUE 1 (LIST (50%)) EMPTY EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the pension position of the special period, of 16.9.2020` 0.5 EQUALS 0.35
#ASSERT `sick days taken off the balance, of 16.9.2020` 10 EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `sick pay in the special period, of 16.9.2020` 500 350 EQUALS 350
#ASSERT `the contributions on the special payment of 16.9.2020` TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST "קרן השתלמות"
#ASSERT `a student's share of a position for the special payment` (LIST 100, 80, 90) 180 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the special payment of 16.9.2020` 10000 30 30 1 PLUS `the birth-pay grant of 16.9.2020` (`the special payment of 16.9.2020` 10000 30 30 1) EQUALS 10000.2

